  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Nartuby runs through Draguignan, Trans-en-Provence and La Motte before joining the Argens, offering several waterfalls and natural pools to cool off in. A Himalayan suspension bridge, confirmed by the tourist office (visitvar.com) — 70 metres long, about 30 metres above the river — spans the gorges at Trans-en-Provence, as part of the "Boucle panoramique du Calant" (1.5 km from the village centre, returning via the Pont de la Motte), free access all year round.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Unlike the big Verdon lakes, the mood here is more intimate and wild — perfect for a dog that prefers small, calm streams to large, busy expanses of water.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the suspension bridge gives an impressive view of the water below — be careful if your dog isn't keen on heights.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Lac de Carcès is about twenty minutes away to extend the freshwater outing.</p>
